<title>FRANCE: Axa says no lay-offs in UAP merger.</title>
<headline>Axa says no lay-offs in UAP merger.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>French insurers Axa and UAP said on Tuesday their merger would not lead to layoffs.</p>
<p>Axa chairman Claude Bebear and Jacques Friedmann stressed on several occasions when pressed by reporters at a news conference that there would be no collective layoffs.</p>
<p>&quot;There will be no collective layoffs, we will show that we can carry out a big merger without collective layoffs,&quot; said Bebear. Axa had carried out major acquisitions in the past which proved it was capable of big deals without layoffs, he said.</p>
<p>&quot;We have said it, this entire operation will be carried out without layoffs,&quot; said Bebear. He added that Axa staff totalled close to 10,000 while UAP staff totalled around 18,000.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
